Thought: How about a potion miscibility table. By this I mean that if you drink
two potions in the course of one turn, they could react with each other and
cause a strange and unpredictable side effect. Like drinking a potion of
healing and then a potion of poison (by mistake, of course). The results could
be as good as resistance to poison to 6d6 explosion (in your stomache). This
could be expanded a bit. The possibility that something will happen drops from
5% to 3% in one turn. Mixing more than two will cause it to increase to 7%.
This way if you drink 5 potions in one turn, you have a 15% or so chance of
something happening. 


